---
const engagements = [
  {
    sector: 'Justice',
    title: 'Booking platform, rebuilt around integrity',
    description:
      'A booking system enabled the very errors it was meant to prevent. Courtrooms were double-booked, past-dated bookings went through, and conflicts went unchecked. The structural issue was the absence of transactional integrity, validation rules, and database constraints. The system was rebuilt to embed all three.',
    outcome:
      'Duplicate bookings disappeared. Hearings stayed on schedule and rescheduling costs vanished.',
  },
  {
    sector: 'Events',
    title: 'Regional events, redesigned around self-service',
    description:
      'For several years, five students, one per region, spent each summer reading emails and manually entering events. The structural issue was the absence of a standardised input format and shared foundation. A form was designed for event organisers to fill out themselves, an automated import loaded the data daily, and an approval mechanism handled review and editing.',
    outcome:
      'What used to be a summer job became a single click.',
  },
  {
    sector: 'Public Administration',
    title: 'Publishing system, built around SDG compliance',
    description:
      'The EU Single Digital Gateway required administrative information to be available in a structured, multilingual, and machine-readable format, crawlable for EU infrastructure. The structural issue was the absence of an editorial foundation for producing this kind of content. A publishing system was designed around predefined form fields, which editors filled out to create or update entries. Metadata tagging, publication, and a structured translation workflow for German and English content were handled automatically in the background.',
    outcome:
      'The first application of its kind in the public sector at the time.',
  },
];
---

<section
  id="selected-engagements"
  class="py-20 sm:py-26 xl:py-36 bg-surface-base"
  aria-labelledby="selected-engagements-heading"
>
  <div class="max-w-300 mx-auto px-gutter xl:px-0">
    <header class="max-w-160 mb-14">
      <p class="font-sans text-sm font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-brand-primary m-0 mb-4">
        Where the approach was built
      </p>
      <h2
        id="selected-engagements-heading"
        data-speakable
        class="font-sans text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold leading-none tracking-tight text-balance break-words hyphens-auto m-0"
      >
        Selected engagements
      </h2>
    </header>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {engagements.map((engagement) => (
        <article class="flex flex-col bg-surface-base border border-ink-primary/10 rounded-md p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="font-sans text-sm font-extrabold tracking-wider uppercase text-brand-primary m-0 mb-3">
            {engagement.sector}
          </p>
          <h3 class="font-sans text-xl md:text-2xl font-extrabold leading-tight tracking-normal break-words hyphens-auto m-0 mb-4 text-ink-primary">
            {engagement.title}
          </h3>
          <p class="font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted m-0 mb-4 flex-1">
            {engagement.description}
          </p>
          {engagement.outcome && (
            <p class="font-sans text-sm text-ink-muted m-0 mt-auto">
              {engagement.outcome}
            </p>
          )}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
